RF.put("questb:b7",{"97287":{"id":97287,"t":"Shrewd negotiations","lv":33,"min":24,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak with Archmage Celindra in the City of Dalaran.\nProvided: Arcane Mote","desc":"You have done well to infiltrate the city of mages, but I believe it is time for us to be more... negotiatory.\nAs much as it pains me to admit, there is no other place on Azeroth with such a vast knowledge of the arcane. My brilliant work still pales in comparison to the ancient wisdom the Kirin Tor have amassed over the years. I think it's high time we are granted access to this exclusive order, don't you think?\nTake the mote you acquired. They will surely give anything to get it back. Anything.\nLevel 33 , requires level 24 Difficulty 24 29 31 36 42 Side Horde Quest ID 97287\nThe chain\n3 quests from level 33 to 34, 9,940 XP in all.\n1 [ 34 ] Blood in the Streets\nFind a way into Dalaran along the Lordamere Lake.\nMagus Wordeen Voidglare Hillsbrad Foothills\n270 XP\n2 [ 33 ] Heart of Disruption\nCollect the Arcane Mote in the City of Dalaran for Magus Wordeen Voidglare in Tarren Mill.\nImage of Archmage Modera Silverpine Forest\n9,400 XP\n3 [ 33 ] Shrewd Negotiations this quest\nSpeak with Archmage Celindra in the City of Dalaran.\n270 XP","cats":["alterac-mountains"]},"7367":{"id":7367,"t":"Defusing the Threat","lv":60,"min":51,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 6,600 experience instead of 9,550, 0.69 times as much.","obj":"Find the Frostwolf Explosives Expert and kill him. Return to the Stormpike Explosives Expert when the task is complete.\nFrostwolf Explosives Expert slain","desc":"The Frostwolf have their front lines and bases booby trapped, ‹class›. You have to watch your step when invading enemy territory.\nIf you want to make a solid strike against them, you must destroy their source of anti personnel munitions - I'm talking about their explosives expert. If you kill him, you are safe to disarm the mines. As long as he is kept down, the mines will also stay down.\nYou will probably find him in a tower near the Iceblood Garrison. Good luck!","rew":"Experience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Stormpike Guard\n+100 reputation with Ironforge\nLevel 60 , requires level 51 Difficulty 51 56 58 Side Alliance Type PvP Shareable Yes Quest ID 7367","cats":["alterac-valley"]},"8167":{"id":8167,"t":"The Battle for Arathi Basin!","lv":35,"min":30,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Assault the mine, the lumber mill, the blacksmith and the farm, then return to Field Marshal Oslight in Refuge Pointe.\nMine Assaulted\nLumber Mill Assaulted\nBlacksmith Assaulted\nFarm Assaulted","desc":"‹name›, the battle for Arathi Basin is a battle for resources and territory. Key points in the area must be held and operated in order to supply our forces with much needed raw materials and supplies. I charge you to assault the points farthest from our Arathi Basin base.\nAssault the farm, the mine, the lumber mill and the blacksmith when they are controlled by the enemy. Find the enemy's banner and rip it from its flag post!\nWhen you have done this to all four points, return to me.","rew":"Money: 75 0 gold, 75 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,750\n+200 reputation with The League of Arathor","pins":[{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":45.8,"y":45.5,"n":"Field Marshal Oslight","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["arathi-basin"]},"247":{"id":247,"t":"The Hunt Completed","lv":30,"min":20,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","rew":"You will receive:\nWildhunter Cloak\nExperience: 3,050\n+150 reputation with Thunder Bluff","done":"‹name›, you have slain all three beasts that comprise the Ashenvale Hunt. You have brought me adequate proof of their demise; there is no question of your strength and tenacity. The blood of a hunter streaks through your veins, and you should be commended!\nPlease, accept this bauble as a sign of congratulations on your mighty deeds done in Ashenvale for the Horde today. May your ancestors watch over you!","pins":[{"z":"Ashenvale","x":73.8,"y":61.5,"n":"Senani Thunderheart","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ashenvale"]},"727":{"id":727,"t":"To Ironforge for Yagyin's Digest","lv":40,"min":30,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Give the Sigil of the Hammer to Gerrig Bonegrip in the Forlorn Cavern of Ironforge.\nSigil of the Hammer\nProvided: Sigil of the Hammer","desc":"The Tablet tells much. But not enough! Not nearly enough!\nThere is a book, a digest that Yagyin wrote in ages past. The ... people I fled ... they keep this book in many places. And their most learned study it. It holds vast knowledge. Knowledge to protect us!\nGo to Gerrig Bonegrip. He is in a shop in Ironforge, in the Forlorn Cavern. Show him this sigil and he'll think you one of them. Ask him for Yagyin's Digest ... and bring it to me!","rew":"Experience: 775","back":"Hello. Welcome to my shop, but watch what you touch.\nKnowledge can be deadly.","done":"Oh. Greetings, brother.\nAnd praise to the dwellers beneath.\nBadlands Dun Morogh","pins":[{"z":"Badlands","x":51.4,"y":76.9,"n":"Theldurin the Lost","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":59.2,"y":22,"n":"Gerrig Bonegrip","e":1}],"cats":["badlands"]},"5047":{"id":5047,"t":"Finkle Einhorn, At Your Service!","lv":60,"min":57,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 57 instead of 55. Gives 6,600 experience instead of 7,050, 0.94 times as much.","obj":"Talk to Malyfous Darkhammer in Everlook.\nGlowing Hunk of the Beast's Flesh\nProvided: Glowing Hunk of the Beast's Flesh","desc":"You'll find Malyfous Darkhammer in Everlook, ‹class›. Tell him that 'Finkle is A-OK' and that the suit works perfectly.\nThen hand him this:\n<Finkle hands you a glowing piece of flesh.>\nI snatched it from the beast's innards during my 'vacation.'\nI bet Malyfous could give you a fairly accurate assessment of what he can do with parts from a monster like this!\nOh, I suppose you don't know where Everlook is, do you? To Winterspring, <fella/lady>!","rew":"Experience: 6,600","back":"Yea?","done":"Alive? Suit worked? And what do we have here?","pins":[{"z":"Winterspring","x":61,"y":38.8,"n":"Malyfous Darkhammer","e":1}],"cats":["blackrock-spire"]},"5127":{"id":5127,"t":"The Demon Forge","lv":60,"min":55,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Travel to Blackrock Spire and find Goraluk Anvilcrack. Slay him and then use the Blood Stained Pike upon his corpse. After his soul has been siphoned, the pike will be Soul Stained.\nYou must also find the Unforged Rune Covered Breastplate.\nReturn both the Soul Stained Pike and the Unforged Rune Covered Breastplate to Lorax in Winterspring.\nSoul Stained Pike\nUnforged Rune Covered Breastplate Unforged Runic Breastplate\nProvided: Blood Stained Pike","desc":"Lorax makes deals, he does not accept them from insignificant mortals.\nA deal I shall make with you, however... take this pike, it is imbued with powerful Fel energies. When you find Goraluk Anvilcrack, slay him and drive this pike through his dying heart. His soul he bartered, his soul I shall have. Return the pike and return the breastplate that the thief stole and I shall teach you what it is that he was to learn.","rew":"You will receive:\nPlans: Demon Forged Breastplate 5 Potion of Demon Slaying Demon Kissed Sack\nExperience: 8,300","back":"Tempt not...","done":"Our pact you did not break. The soul I did take. The reward I shall make.","pins":[{"z":"Winterspring","x":63.8,"y":73.8,"n":"Lorax","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["blackrock-spire"]},"97927":{"id":97927,"t":"Camping 101 alchemy","lv":6,"min":4,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak with Kray in Thunder Bluff to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.\nRaise your alchemy skill to 20","desc":"So, you chose to cook up brews and potions as an Alchemist. I'm sure that'll come in handy in your travels.\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a Mana Well for your camp. Build one of these and all of the healers and spellcaster types will come running to get a refreshing taste.","done":"There you have it, you can now craft your very own Mana Well. Most folk don't care much for camps being set up in the center of town, so you'll need to head into the wilderness if you want to test it out.\nOh, and just remember, no camp is complete without a campfire. You'll need one of those before you start up your camp. Most cooks can teach you to make a fire. If you haven't already, you might want to check in with someone who can train you in the culinary arts to learn the basics.\nMulgore Thunder Bluff","pins":[{"z":"Mulgore","x":46.2,"y":67.2,"n":"Kaga Wildhoof","s":1},{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":46.8,"y":34.2,"n":"Kray","e":1}],"cats":["camping"]},"94247":{"id":94247,"t":"Craftsmans writ lesser wizards robe","min":1,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Lesser Wizard's Robe\nLesser Wizard's Robe","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting $2oa Lesser Wizard's Robe, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>","back":"<The man stands at attention, peering over the mountainside toward Dalaran. He regards your presence with a subtle wave of a hand, beckoning you closer.>","done":"<Alan speaks in a whisper.>\nDon't you think it is a little suspicious to be carrying elegant robes in broad daylight to a man garbed in dark leathers?\nWell, ahem, fortunately I am out here on behalf of the Kirin Tor, so there is no shady transaction about to take place. None at all.\nThe robe, please.","pins":[{"z":"Alterac Mountains","x":30.4,"y":61.2,"n":"Alan Sneeks","e":1}],"cats":["crafting"]},"94327":{"id":94327,"t":"Craftsmans writ orcish war leggings","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Orcish War Leggings\nOrcish War Leggings","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting $2oa Orcish War Leggings, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>\nStart an item: Craftsman's Writ: Orcish War Leggings Level 0 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 3 Side Both factions Quest ID 94327","cats":["crafting"]},"7927":{"id":7927,"t":"Darkmoon Portals Deck","lv":55,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Return the Portals Deck to the Darkmoon Faire when it comes to town.\nPortals Deck","desc":"Now that you have gathered all of the Portal cards together into a deck, a ninth card mysteriously appears with the same backing as the first eight. On this card is inscribed, \"Return these cards to the Darkmoon Faire and be rewarded.\" You have heard that this faire alternately stops at Mulgore and Goldshire every few months, so you will have to wait until they are here next.","rew":"You will receive:\nDarkmoon Card: Twisting Nether\nExperience: 550\n+150 reputation with Darkmoon Faire","back":"I see that you have managed to complete a deck of portals! Congratulations!","done":"So you have put together a deck of Portals. Your gesture of returning it to us will create a tie between you and the Darkmoon that will not soon be forgotten. Allow me to present you with one of the greater darkmoon cards as a small token of our appreciation.\nMulgore Elwynn Forest","pins":[{"z":"Mulgore","x":37.4,"y":45,"n":"Professor Thaddeus Paleo","e":1},{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":41.3,"y":70.1,"n":"Professor Thaddeus Paleo","e":1}],"cats":["darkmoon-faire"]},"4727":{"id":4727,"t":"Beached Sea Turtle","lv":15,"min":12,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take the Sea Turtle Remains to Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde in Auberdine.\nSea Turtle Remains Skeletal Sea Turtle\nProvided: Sea Turtle Remains","desc":"The skeletal remains of a sea turtle lie in the sand of the northern Darkshore beaches. The Greymist murlocs have either not found this carcass, or perhaps they have and are shying away from it for some unknown reason. Regardless, there is enough of the turtle left to take a sample back to Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde in Auberdine for the Temple of the Moon to study.","rew":"Money: 3 50 0 gold, 3 silver, 50 copper Experience: 550\n+50 reputation with Darnassus","back":"Hello again, ‹name›! Are you here to report on another discovery?","done":"You've found even more beached creatures, ‹name›? Sea turtles were commonly found frolicking along the base of Nordrassil before it was destroyed. With the birth of Teldrassil, however, these creatures have been seen in ever decreasing numbers. Some, as we have discovered, end their lives here for some unknown reason.\nYour aid will perhaps unlock the mystery before us. Please accept this in exchange for the remains you have provided for our study.","pins":[{"z":"Darkshore","x":53.1,"y":18.1,"n":"Beached Sea Turtle","s":1},{"z":"Darkshore","x":36.6,"y":45.6,"n":"Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde","e":1}],"cats":["darkshore"]},"967":{"id":967,"t":"The Tower of Althalaxx","lv":18,"min":13,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Deliver Balthule's letter to Delgren the Purifier in Ashenvale Forest.\nLetter to Delgren\nProvided: Letter to Delgren","desc":"My master, Delgren the Purifier, is a paladin who has graciously offered his assistance in defending our forests from the forces of the demons and undead. He has taught me much about the Holy Light and the art of battle.\nDelgren must know of the cult's operations immediately.\nYou will find him far south of here at Maestra's Post in Ashenvale Forest. Be swift, I fear the Dark Strand's threat grows with each passing hour.","rew":"Experience: 1,000\n+75 reputation with Darnassus","back":"You have some business with me, ‹class›?","done":"If you don't mind my saying, you seem a bit well-equipped for a messenger, hm? I suppose Balthule wanted to be certain that his letter reached my hands. Let's see what he has to say...\nThis is disturbing news. When undead or demonic forces are found, I help the Sentinels destroy them.\nAt first I was unaccustomed to the manners of the night elves, but I have grown to respect them greatly as allies.\nDarkshore Ashenvale","pins":[{"z":"Darkshore","x":55,"y":24.9,"n":"Balthule Shadowstrike","s":1},{"z":"Ashenvale","x":26.2,"y":38.7,"n":"Delgren the Purifier","e":1}],"cats":["darkshore"]},"98887":{"id":98887,"t":"Conflict at darkspear islands","lv":39,"min":30,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Bring 3 Darkspear Islands Marks of Honor to a Horde Warbringer outside the battlegrounds.\n3 Darkspear Islands Mark of Honor","desc":"The Theramore Expeditionary Force are tenacious and continue to send reinforcements to bolster their position on the Darkspear Islands.\nGo, show them the might of the Horde! Bring me the evidence of your victory in this key battleground and you will be well rewarded.","rew":"Money: 45 0 gold, 45 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,500\n+150 reputation with Darkspear Raiders\nThe Barrens Alterac Mountains Arathi Highlands Undercity Orgrimmar Thunder Bluff","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":46.6,"y":8.6,"n":"Horde Warbringer","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Alterac Mountains","x":63,"y":59.8,"n":"Horde Warbringer","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":73.6,"y":29.2,"n":"Horde Warbringer","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":58.2,"y":97.6,"n":"Horde Warbringer","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":80.4,"y":30.4,"n":"Horde Warbringer","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":57.8,"y":76.8,"n":"Horde Warbringer","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["darkspear-islands"]},"1047":{"id":1047,"t":"The New Frontier","lv":55,"min":54,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Arch Druid Fandral Staghelm at the Cenarion Enclave of Darnassus about the Cenarion Circle's call to explore the frontiers of Kalimdor.","desc":"Attention, heroes!\nThe Cenarion Circle seeks able bodied individuals to assist them in exploring the vast new frontiers of Kalimdor! A forbidden wasteland of unimaginable dangers lies far to the west of Tanaris and Gadgetzan, and the Circle needs willing and honorable proxies to act in their stead.\nAll interested individuals should seek audience with the Cenarion Circle. Speak with the Arch Druid in Darnassus, Fandral Staghelm, for more information!","rew":"Experience: 550","done":"What makes you think I wish to be pestered by the likes of you, ‹class›? Wait - let me stop the important duties I attend to on a daily basis so I can help you locate a doodad somewhere. By all means, the welfare of Darnassus - nay, all of Teldrassil - should come second to the acquisition of a bauble for your collection.\nThe fools in Moonglade waste my time with their call for assistance, and now I must endure this?","pins":[{"z":"Darnassus","x":47.8,"y":82,"n":"Herald Moonstalker","s":1},{"z":"Darnassus","x":34.8,"y":9.3,"n":"Arch Druid Fandral Staghelm","e":1}],"cats":["darnassus"]},"1367":{"id":1367,"t":"Magram Alliance","lv":33,"min":30,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Gain a Friendly reputation with the Magram, then speak with Warug.\nReach 3000 reputation with Magram Clan Centaur","desc":"To beat the centaur, we must use their hatred against them. We will ally with one of the clans and through them, we will learn how to defeat all the clans.\nIf you choose to ally with the Magram then slay their foes, the Gelkis. This will earn you respect among the Magram. When you earn enough, then meet with the Magram spokesman Warug, on the outskirts of the Magram Village, in southeast Desolace.","rew":"Experience: 650\n-500 reputation with Gelkis Clan Centaur\n+100 reputation with Magram Clan Centaur","back":"Leave! The Magram do not speak with the weak. We kill them!\nIf you want to speak with me, then show me you are strong. Return after you slay many Gelkis.","done":"The Gelkis cry when they hear your name, ‹name›. They fear you and they hate you. They hate you like they hate the Magram!\nMaybe you are strong like the Magram. We will see...","pins":[{"z":"Desolace","x":56.3,"y":59.7,"n":"Gurda Wildmane","s":1},{"z":"Desolace","x":75,"y":68.2,"n":"Warug","e":1}],"cats":["desolace"]},"8967":{"id":8967,"t":"The Left Piece of Lord Valthalak's Amulet","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Use the Brazier of Beckoning to summon forth the spirit of Isalien and slay her. Return to Bodley inside Blackrock Mountain with the Left Piece of Lord Valthalak's Amulet and the Brazier of Beckoning.\nLeft Piece of Lord Valthalak's Amulet Mor Grayhoof , Isalien , Jarien , Sothos and 1 more\nBrazier of Beckoning\nIsalien slain\nProvided: Brazier of Beckoning","desc":"It became known to us in later days, as we were doing what we could ourselves to survive, that Isalien, a night elf priestess of our company, had gone to the night elvic ancestral city, now known as Dire Maul. From what we gathered, she went there both for personal reasons and also to unlock the secrets of the piece of the amulet that she had in her possession.\nShe didn't quite make it, though. Word got back to us that she was ambushed at the Shrine of Eldretharr by Alzzin the Wildshaper and his forces.","rew":"Experience: 8,300","back":"Surely you haven't already dealt with the salvation of Isalien's spirit and the retrieval of the left piece of Lord Valthalak's amulet, ‹name›?","done":"Thank you, ‹name›, for putting Isalien's spirit to rest. Now, perhaps, she will find peace with her goddess. But, there is still a great deal of work ahead of us if we are to get out of this fine pickle we find ourselves in.\nUnfortunately, I do not know the location of the one who died with the right piece of the amulet in their possession. But do not fear; in life I was a dabbler in the art of divination, so I have another task for you, which is going to enable us to ferret out the final piece.","pins":[{"z":"Burning Steppes","x":32.3,"y":25.8,"n":"Bodley","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["dire-maul"]},"5927":{"id":5927,"t":"Heeding the Call","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Turak Runetotem on the Elder Rise of Thunder Bluff.","desc":"Excuse me, friend...\nIt has come to my attention that Turak Runetotem has put out word that he wishes to speak with you. It seems that your training as a druid is about to take on a new life, and he will be training you personally. Turak is one of the Arch Druid's assistants; he is known as a wise and patient druid, and he should teach you well.\nHe is located in Thunder Bluff, inside the Cenarion Circle's main tent on the Elder Rise.","rew":"Experience: 85\n+25 reputation with Cenarion Circle","done":"I am glad you found your way here today. young ‹class›. The time has come for you to take a large step into a much larger world.\nInside each of Cenarius' children is the call to serve nature. Animals and plants are our friends as well as our charges. We choose to devote our lives as preservers of balance for their sakes as well as our own. Your first step into this world will be to learn of the ways of the bear, and to learn strength of body and heart.\nReady yourself!\nMulgore Thunder Bluff","pins":[{"z":"Mulgore","x":44.6,"y":76.6,"n":"Gart Mistrunner","s":1},{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":76.5,"y":27.2,"n":"Turak Runetotem","e":1}],"cats":["druid"]},"1287":{"id":1287,"t":"The Deserters","lv":38,"min":30,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Captain Garran Vimes in Theramore about Reethe.","desc":"Reethe? That coward?\nWe threw him out of camp because he insisted on raiding the supplies of the ogres up at Brackenwall Village. We're not so many in number that we could stand up to those mindless brutes.\nHe crossed the line one too many times, so we left him to fend for himself.\nNow, I helped you out... So, why don't you help us out and forget you bumped into us?","rew":"Experience: 2,850","done":"I will send Lieutenant Caldwell to deal with the deserters at Lost Point. In addition, I will instruct him to find Reethe. The marsh is not so big and trackless that he should be unable to find him.","pins":[{"z":"Dustwallow Marsh","x":36.1,"y":54.3,"n":"Balos Jacken","s":1},{"z":"Dustwallow Marsh","x":68.2,"y":48.6,"n":"Captain Garran Vimes","e":1}],"cats":["dustwallow-marsh"]},"9127":{"id":9127,"t":"Bone Fragments","lv":60,"min":55,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"30 Bone Fragments Lord Darkscythe 89.3 % , Skul 57 % in Stratholme , Vectus 50 % in Scholomance , Rattlegore 48 % in Scholomance and 4 more","rew":"You will receive:\nInsignia of the Crusade\nMoney: 9 0 gold, 9 silver, 0 copper\n+10 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"A man in my line of work can never have too many bone fragments, ‹name›. Whenever you have a surplus of fragments, bring them to me and I'll reward you with another insignia.","done":"My dream of becoming a full-time dancer at the Gadgetzan disco is soon to become a reality! Keep up the good work, ‹name›.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.6,"y":48.9,"n":"Rohan the Assassin","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["eastern-plaguelands"]},"7":{"id":7,"t":"Kobold Camp Cleanup","lv":2,"min":1,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Kill 10 Kobold Vermin, then return to Marshal McBride.\nKobold Vermin slain : 0/ 10","desc":"Your first task is one of cleansing, ‹name›. A clan of kobolds have infested the woods to the north. Go there and fight the kobold vermin you find. Reduce their numbers so that we may one day drive them from Northshire.","rew":"Money: 25 0 gold, 0 silver, 25 copper Experience: 170\n+100 reputation with Stormwind","back":"How goes the hunting, ‹name›? Have you found and defeated those vermin?","done":"Well done, citizen. Those kobolds are thieves and cowards, but in large numbers they pose a threat to us. And the humans of Stormwind do not need another threat.\nFor defeating them, you have my gratitude.","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":48.9,"y":41.6,"n":"Marshal McBride","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["elwynn-forest"]},"99127":{"id":99127,"t":"A net disaster","lv":7,"min":4,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Check the fishing traps in Crystal Lake.\n7 Half-Eaten Fish","desc":"The fish just ain't biting today, and there's something wrong going on with them. It's not just empty hooks. I haven't seen a single minnow up in the water at all.\nLee here set up some traps overnight, go check to see if we've at least got some stock there. If you find anything weird, make sure to show me.","back":"Any catches to speak of?","done":"All the traps are like this? Seems our new neighboring nuisances are causing more destruction than we were aware of. I'll go broke if we don't do something about it.","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":47.4,"y":62.2,"n":"Jason Mathers","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["elwynn-forest"]},"87":{"id":87,"t":"Goldtooth","lv":8,"min":5,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Bernice's Necklace to \"Auntie\" Bernice Stonefield at the Stonefield Farm.\nBernice's Necklace Goldtooth","desc":"I was playing near the Fargodeep Mine, and I think I dropped, er...I mean I saw, the old lady's necklace. Don't ask me how it got there...it wasn't me!\nWell anyway, I saw this big, gold-toothed kobold pick up the necklace and run into the mine. Go find that kobold and you'll find the necklace, I swear!","rew":"You will receive:\nLion-stamped Gloves\nExperience: 875\n+150 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Hello, ‹name›. Have you found my necklace?","done":"Oh, you found it! Thank you, thank you dear!\nHere, take this. It was my husband's and he always said it was lucky. If only he didn't forget it on his last campaign! *sniff*","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":43.1,"y":85.7,"n":"Billy Maclure","s":1},{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":34.5,"y":84.3,"n":"\"Auntie\" Bernice Stonefield","e":1}],"cats":["elwynn-forest"]},"3127":{"id":3127,"t":"Mountain Giant Muisek","lv":50,"min":40,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Kill 7 Land Walkers or Cliff Giants. Use the Muisek Vessel to shrink and capture the fallen Mountain Giants.\n7 Mountain Giant Muisek\nMountain Giant Muisek Vessel\nProvided: Mountain Giant Muisek Vessel","desc":"The last task I will require of you is to travel to the northwest and find the final enemy.\nThe mountain giants left the mountains to aid the night elves when the burning legion appeared in the world. You will know them by their massive size and the way the ground begins to shake as you travel along their rocky terrain.\nI am eager to harness power of that size. Kill 7 mountain giants, then use the muisek vessel to capture their powerful muisek.","rew":"Experience: 4,700\n+100 reputation with Darkspear Trolls","back":"Were you able to capture the mountain giants?","done":"Just imagine the possibilities of what we now possess, ‹name›. Along with the materials that you have collected, I will be able to forever trap the muisek of these creatures into whatever I wish.","pins":[{"z":"Feralas","x":74.4,"y":43.4,"n":"Witch Doctor Uzer'i","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["feralas"]},"567":{"id":567,"t":"Dangerous!","lv":28,"min":19,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"High Executor Darthalia of Tarren Mill is offering a bounty on Clerk Horrace Whitesteed, Citizen Wilkes, Miner Hackett and Farmer Kalaba.\nClerk Horrace Whitesteed slain\nCitizen Wilkes slain\nMiner Hackett slain\nFarmer Kalaba slain","desc":"Dangerous!\nThe following humans of Hillsbrad have been deemed dangerous and are marked for bounty by High Executor Darthalia:\nClerk Horrace Whitesteed. Wanted for the murder of Deathguard Toma.\nCitizen Wilkes. Wanted for the murder of Apothecary Eli.\nMiner Hackett. Wanted for the murder of Deathstalker Fry.\nFarmer Kalaba. Wanted for the ambush of supplies from the Undercity.\nAll of these enemies are hiding and will be hard to find. A reward will be granted upon notice of their death.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nBow of Plunder Sentry Buckler Charred Wand\nYou will also receive:\nHooded Cowl\nExperience: 2,300\n+100 reputation with Undercity","back":"Yes?","done":"You are quite the bounty hunter, ‹class›. Well done.","pins":[{"z":"Hillsbrad Foothills","x":62.6,"y":19.7,"n":"Dangerous!","s":1},{"z":"Hillsbrad Foothills","x":62.3,"y":20.5,"n":"High Executor Darthalia","e":1}],"cats":["hillsbrad-foothills"]},"6087":{"id":6087,"t":"Taming the Beast","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Use the Taming Rod to tame a Prairie Stalker. Practice your skills, then return the Taming Rod to Yaw Sharpmane in Bloodhoof Village.\nTaming Rod\nProvided: Taming Rod","desc":"You have a fiery spirit, hunter, readily awaiting your next challenge.\nYour next task is to gain the companionship of a wolf known as the prairie stalker. This creature is swift and fearless; in taking this beast as your pet, you must also take on these qualities.\nDuring a battle, you will learn how you and your pet will become a team. In the end you must work as one, muscle to muscle.\nHere is the taming rod, ‹name›. Tame a prairie stalker and practice your skills.","rew":"Experience: 850","back":"Have you found a prairie stalker?","done":"Yes... The Earthmother believes that you are ready for the next lesson.","pins":[{"z":"Mulgore","x":46.9,"y":59.6,"n":"Yaw Sharpmane","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["hunter"]},"94007":{"id":94007,"t":"Taming the beast","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Report to Quel'ana Quickgale in Valanaar.","desc":"Now that you've gained a level of comfort in the wilds of the highlands, I believe it is time for you to seek your very own animal companion.\nGo to the port of Valanaar to the southeast, and speak with Quel'ana Quickgale there. He will instruct you in the art of beast taming.","done":"I am most glad that you came. Come, let us begin.","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":45.2,"y":44.2,"n":"Elayaa Easewind","s":1},{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":59.6,"y":72.6,"n":"Quel'ana Quickgale","e":1}],"cats":["hunter"]},"8647":{"id":8647,"t":"Bellowrage the Elder","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","rew":"You will receive:\nCoin of Ancestry\n+50 reputation with Horde\n+50 reputation with Alliance","done":"It is good to know the people of this land still pay homage to the olden races. I bid you well, ‹name›, and offer you this token...","pins":[{"z":"Blasted Lands","x":57.9,"y":54.9,"n":"Elder Bellowrage","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["lunar-festival"]},"8727":{"id":8727,"t":"Farwhisper the Elder","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","rew":"You will receive:\nCoin of Ancestry\n+50 reputation with Horde\n+50 reputation with Alliance","done":"The heavens, in their countless stars, hold answers to earthly mysteries, ‹name›. Might, then, the wise, and the lucky, gaze up and find truth?\nStart Elder Farwhisper Stratholme End Elder Farwhisper Stratholme Level 60 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 56 58 Side Both factions Shareable Yes Quest ID 8727","cats":["lunar-festival"]},"9367":{"id":9367,"t":"The Festival of Fire","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 650 experience instead of 150, 4.33 times as much.","obj":"Touch the bonfires within Stormwind, Ironforge, and Darnassus, then speak to a Festival Loremaster within the capital cities.\nFlame of Stormwind used\nFlame of Ironforge used\nFlame of Darnassus used","desc":"Midsummer is upon us once again!\nEach year, as tradition dictates, Flamekeepers are chosen to tend the bonfires within our capitals. While fires are burning throughout Azeroth, it is imperative that ours be the hottest and brightest, to properly pay homage to the season.\nIn fact, I have a task for you, if you don't mind. I've not yet heard if the fires in all capitals are properly burning. Travel there yourself and warm yourself by the fires--make sure they're hot!","rew":"You will receive:\n10 Burning Blossom 10 Fiery Festival Brew\nExperience: 650","back":"Are the fires burning?","done":"Excellent! It seems we've appointed dutiful Flamekeepers this year if the bonfires are as well-kept as you claim. Thank you for inspecting them for me; here, take this as a small token of my esteem.\nTeldrassil Dun Morogh Stormwind City","pins":[{"z":"Teldrassil","x":56.5,"y":92.2,"n":"Festival Loremaster","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":61.3,"y":25.1,"n":"Festival Loremaster","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":50,"y":72,"n":"Festival Loremaster","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["midsummer"]},"5527":{"id":5527,"t":"A Reliquary of Purity","lv":60,"min":56,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Travel to Silithus and search for a Reliquary of Purity within the ruins of Southwind Village. If you are able to find it, return with it to Rabine Saturna in Nighthaven, Moonglade.\nReliquary of Purity Dusty Reliquary","desc":"The first step is to find a container capable of holding an extremely corruptible substance without the handler suffering ill effects. There is only one sort device I am aware of that could possibly contain something as vile as the Felvine: a Reliquary of Purity.\nDeep in the wasteland of Silithus is the remnants of the night elf village known as Southwind. I know one was there many, many years ago. If we are to succeed, I need you to scour those ruins in the hopes of reclaiming it.","rew":"Experience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Cenarion Circle","back":"A Reliquary of Purity is an artifact unto itself. Few were ever made, and almost all of them were thought to have been lost over time.\nI admit I have known about the one in Southwind for a little while now. Honestly, with the rising turmoil in Silithus, I thought to keep our secrets just that - a secret. To poke and prod would only cause suspicions of our enemies to rise.\nAlas, the time for complacency is at an end, especially with the situation in Eldre'Thalas.","done":"Indeed, you are as resourceful as many claim. The Cenarion Circle is blessed to have you working in our stead.\nWith the Reliquary once more in our hands, my mind is at ease. I feel more comfortable asking you to not only face down a malfeasant demon, but also to bring back a dangerous item in the process...\nMoonglade Silithus","pins":[{"z":"Moonglade","x":51.7,"y":45.1,"n":"Rabine Saturna","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["moonglade"]},"9047":{"id":9047,"t":"Redemption Boots","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Commander Eligor Dawnbringer at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands will make Redemption Boots if you bring him the following: 1 Desecrated Boots, 12 Wartorn Plate Scraps, 2 Arcanite Bars and 3 Cured Rugged Hides.\nDesecrated Boots Gluth 0 % in Naxxramas , Gothik the Harvester 0 % in Naxxramas , Instructor Razuvious 0 % in Naxxramas\n12 Wartorn Plate Scrap Infectious Ghoul 22.5 % in Naxxramas , Stoneskin Gargoyle 21.6 % in Naxxramas , Plagued Deathhound 21.3 % in Naxxramas , Mad Scientist 20.8 % in Naxxramas and 4 more\n2 Arcanite Bar\n3 Cured Rugged Hide","desc":"You will find the remnants of our fallen heroes on the corpses of the Lords of Naxxramas. Bring those desecrated keepsakes to me along with wartorn plate scraps and crafting materials capable of revitalizing the cursed armor and I shall craft a fine piece of armor for you.","rew":"You will receive:\nRedemption Boots\n+200 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"You got some missing parts for the quest please go and get them all!","done":"Exellent ‹name› !\n, you got everything just as i asked and now i can make a Redemption Boots.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.7,"y":48.6,"n":"Commander Eligor Dawnbringer","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["naxxramas"]},"6567":{"id":6567,"t":"The Champion of the Horde","lv":60,"min":55,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 3,300 experience instead of 3,650, 0.9 times as much.","obj":"Seek out Rexxar. The Warchief has instructed you as to his whereabouts. Search the paths of Desolace, between the Stonetalon Mountains and Feralas.","desc":"I have received word from one of my champions that a way into the lair of the dragon may exist. You are to seek him out.\nRexxar wanders the desert wasteland of Desolace, traveling between Stonetalon and Feralas. He awaits your arrival.","rew":"Experience: 3,300","done":"There is but one way into the dragon's lair, ‹race›.\nYou see, only the strongest of the Black Dragonflight are allowed entry into the lair of the brood mother. Many trials must be passed and the key to enter ceremoniously enchanted by General Drakkisath himself!\nSince you are not of black dragonkin, you may have some difficulty in obtaining passage.\n<Rexxar grins.>\nOrgrimmar Feralas","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":31.7,"y":37.8,"n":"Thrall","s":1},{"z":"Feralas","x":46.4,"y":18.2,"n":"Rexxar","e":1}],"cats":["orgrimmar"]},"98407":{"id":98407,"t":"Show of force","lv":17,"min":11,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Collect 5 Spiked Collars from Gnoll Thrashers for Deputy Feldon near Lakeshire.\n5 Spiked Collar","desc":"If the gnolls are growing so bold they are willing to camp this close to humans, there's no telling how much further they'll go. We need to deter them.\nThe beasts are hardly organized, but they seem to respect strength above all else. If we can slay the worst of them, maybe claim some of their trophies, we can remind these gnolls why they should stay in the hills where they belong.\nShould you see any of their thrashers, bring me their collars. That should put the fear of the Alliance back into them.","back":"A full assessment of the gnolls cannot be complete without facing the worst of their kind. Put those thrashers down!","done":"Quite the armful you have.\nWhile this doesn't solve our problem out here, I can rest comfortably knowing we've discouraged them pushing any further. Great work, ‹name›.","pins":[{"z":"Redridge Mountains","x":30.8,"y":60,"n":"Deputy Feldon","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["redridge-mountains"]},"98247":{"id":98247,"t":"Shipping label","lv":60,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Deliver the Shipping Label to someone at the Azeroth Commerce Authority trade hub in Redridge Mountains.\nShipping Label","desc":"<A torn shipping label can be found on the side of the now fully stocked crate. Though the intended recipient is torn off, details of its origin still remain.\n\"Property of the Azeroth Commerce Authority. Please return empty crates or unfulfilled shipments to our local trade hub at the Three Corners crossroads in Redridge Mountains. Couriers will be compensated for their time and travel.\"\nBeside the text is a crudely drawn map of the area near the aforementioned destination.>","back":"Ah, greetings! How can I be of assistance?","done":"You have arrived at the right place! I am happy to mark you down as one of our affiliates. No contracts to sign and no commitments to weigh you down. All we ask of you is your diligence to assist in completing or returning any of our deliveries you find on your travels.\nWhen you do so, you will be compensated with Merchant's Favor that will allow you to purchase goods and services we offer here. In fact, here's a little bit to get you started.\nNow, do you happen to have the crate this came from?","pins":[{"z":"Redridge Mountains","x":9.6,"y":71,"n":"Marcy Baker","e":1}],"cats":["redridge-mountains"]},"3367":{"id":3367,"t":"Suntara Stones","lv":48,"min":40,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Help Dorius get back to Ironforge.","desc":"<Dorius groans.>\nI'm badly injured, ‹race›. Feel... light headed... World spinning... Bleeding... internally.\nI must get back to Ironforge. Help me, ‹name›.","rew":"Experience: 4,400\n+100 reputation with Ironforge","back":"I'm not going to make it...","done":"This letter was dropped by Dorius when he was shot.","pins":[{"z":"Searing Gorge","x":63.9,"y":61,"n":"Dorius Stonetender","s":1},{"z":"Searing Gorge","x":74.4,"y":19.3,"n":"Singed Letter","e":1}],"cats":["searing-gorge"]},"1527":{"id":1527,"t":"Call of Fire","lv":13,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. New rewards: Totem of Charged Flames.","obj":"Bring the Torch of Eternal Flame to Kranal Fiss in the Barrens.\nTorch of the Eternal Flame\nProvided: Torch of the Eternal Flame","desc":"Torch firmly in hand, you turn away from the brazier and look out over Durotar. You feel an excitement tugging at your spirit as the wind picks up and forces the flame to dance violently.\nYou start off down the path back to the Barrens in search of Kranal Fiss.","rew":"New in Forever: Totem of Charged Flames.\nYou will receive:\nFire Totem Totem of Charged Flames\nYou will learn: Searing Totem\nExperience: 1,150","back":"Yes, ‹name›? What do you have there?","done":"Your spirit burns brighter than any torch I've ever seen, ‹name›, and for that, you should be proud.\nIf you continue down this path, the elements will be yours to command, and our brethren will look to you for guidance and wisdom. Let me be the first to congratulate you and present to you your newest totem.\nDurotar The Barrens","pins":[{"z":"Durotar","x":39,"y":58.2,"n":"Brazier of the Dormant Flame","s":1},{"z":"The Barrens","x":56,"y":19.9,"n":"Kranal Fiss","e":1}],"cats":["shaman"]},"8807":{"id":8807,"t":"Scrying Materials","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 1 Large Brilliant Shard, 1 Large Radiant Shard and 1 Huge Emerald to Geologist Larksbane at Cenarion Hold in Silithus. You must also bring Logistics Task Briefing V in order to complete this quest.\nLarge Brilliant Shard\nLarge Radiant Shard\nHuge Emerald Alzzin's Minion 1.2 % , Large Obsidian Chunk 1 % , Small Obsidian Chunk 1 % , Hakkari Thorium Vein 0.9 % and 4 more\nLogistics Task Briefing V\nProvided: Logistics Task Briefing V","desc":"Geologist Larksbane's studies have proven to be of tremendous value to our operations in Silithus. She has recently requested scrying materials to be used in her research.\nPlease gather these materials and deliver them to her directly so that she may continue her research.","rew":"You will receive:\nCenarion Logistics Badge Followup Logistics Assignment\nExperience: 650\n+50 reputation with Cenarion Circle","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":49.7,"y":37.5,"n":"Geologist Larksbane","e":1}],"cats":["silithus"]},"1687":{"id":1687,"t":"Spooky Lighthouse","lv":60,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take the orphan to see the lighthouse off the coast of Westfall.","desc":"Sometimes late at night, our matrons at the orphanage will tell us spooky stories. Those RULE! There's one about a ghost that haunts a lighthouse in Westfall. They say he was a pirate captain who had his ship taken from him by other pirates. Wow!\nCould you please take me to the lighthouse in Westfall? I wanna see if the ghost of that captain is there! I promise to stay close to you; I won't run off or anything!","rew":"Experience: 650\n+50 reputation with Alliance","back":"Are we there yet?","done":"WOW, that was a real life ghost! That was so awesome - I can't wait to tell everyone back at the orphanage. Captain Grayson... he even looked like a pirate! When I grow up I wanna be a ghost pirate too!\nThanks for taking me to Westfall, ‹name›. I know there are scary things out there in the wilds of Westfall, and I hope I wasn't too much of a pain. You're awesome!\nWestfall Open the zone on the world map Start Human Orphan End Human Orphan Level 60 , requires level 10 Difficulty 10 56 58 Side Alliance Shareable No Quest ID 1687\nThe chain\n2 quests at level 60, 650 XP in all.\n1 [ 60 ] Children's Week\nUse the Human Orphan Whistle to talk with the child you will be looking after during Children's Week.\nOrphan Matron Nightingale Stormwind City\n2 [ 60 ] Spooky Lighthouse this quest\nTake the orphan to see the lighthouse off the coast of Westfall.\nHuman Orphan\n650 XP","cats":["special"]},"1447":{"id":1447,"t":"The Missing Diplomat","lv":31,"min":28,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Defeat Dashel Stonefist in Stormwind.","desc":"Yeah, you're obviously not the smartest ‹class› to come into Stormwind, but you're about to be one of the dumbest to never leave.\nHave you met me friends?","rew":"Experience: 1,250\n+50 reputation with Stormwind","back":"I didn't mean anything by the comment 'bout you being a stupid ‹class›. We're friends, right? No hard feelings?","done":"So, you came to me for a reason. What is it you need?","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":74.3,"y":59.2,"n":"Dashel Stonefist","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stormwind-city"]},"97047":{"id":97047,"t":"The cook in the cage","lv":38,"min":30,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Find a key to Wendel's cage, and a disguise for him to sneak out, within the Kurzen compound.\nCompound Cage Key\nKurzen Fighter's Uniform","desc":"Hey! You! You have to help me! I was just out exploring the jungle when, all of a sudden, I was ambushed by these maniacs! I don't know what they plan to do with me, but I've heard talk of tigers and headshrinkers, and I don't want part in either!\nI don't know how, but you have to get me out of here! Please! A key to this cage, a disguise to sneak out, something! Anything!\nStranglethorn Vale Open the zone on the world map Level 38 , requires level 30 Difficulty 30 34 36 41 48 Side Both factions Shareable Yes Quest ID 97047","cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"1127":{"id":1127,"t":"Fool's Stout","lv":44,"min":35,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 35 instead of 36.","obj":"Bring 12 of Zanzil's Mixture to Crank Fizzlebub in Booty Bay.\n12 Zanzil's Mixture Chucky \"Ten Thumbs\" 33 % , Jon-Jon the Crow 33 % , Zanzil the Outcast 33 % , Zanzil Naga 33 % and 3 more","desc":"So you want some Fool's Stout, eh? Thinking of heading back to the races...?\nAll right, bring me more of Zanzil's mixture and I'll make some more stout for you.","rew":"You will receive:\nFool's Stout\nExperience: 210","back":"Do you have those Zanzil mixtures yet, ‹name›?","done":"Ah, very good! Here is your pay.\nAnd here is a little something extra... for your discretion.","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":27.1,"y":77.2,"n":"Crank Fizzlebub","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"3447":{"id":3447,"t":"Secret of the Circle","lv":51,"min":46,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Travel into the Sunken Temple and discover the secret hidden in the circle of statues.","desc":"My memories are cloudy, but I will tell you what I can. The circle of statues in the Sunken Temple, while dangerous, I believe that they hold the secret to unlock an even greater treasure.\nFrom the main altar, I was able to activate a series of lights. I think that if you can uncover what these lights mean, you might be able to unlock whatever secrets are hiding in this room.\nI warn you though, ‹name›. Great evil lies in the temple. It's likely that anything valuable will be fervently guarded...","rew":"You will receive:\nHakkari Urn\nExperience: 6,100","done":"The eye of the idol glitters brightly even in the half-darkness of the temple. Its transparency reveals something shiny behind it. Sliding it to the side, you reach in and grasp what lies inside the statue.\nThe Atal'ai treasure is now yours.","pins":[{"z":"Tanaris","x":52.7,"y":45.9,"n":"Marvon Rivetseeker","s":1}],"cats":["sunken-temple"]},"487":{"id":487,"t":"The Road to Darnassus","lv":8,"min":5,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Slay 6 Gnarlpine Ambushers and return to Sentinel Amara Nightwalker outside of Dolanaar.\nGnarlpine Ambusher slain : 0/ 6","desc":"The road to Darnassus must be kept safe. Travelers heading from Dolanaar to Darnassus have been reporting ruthless attacks by corrupted furbolgs from the Gnarlpine tribe.\nImportant news and commerce travels to and from Darnassus by way of this road daily. We cannot afford to have a rogue band of heathens terrorizing people.\nTake up arms in the name of the sacred forest, ‹class›. Their den lies somewhere below this vantage point. Slay 6 of these Gnarlpine ambushers and report back to me.","rew":"Money: 2 25 0 gold, 2 silver, 25 copper Experience: 700\n+100 reputation with Darnassus","back":"The road is still not safe, ‹class›. Travel forth and slay 6 Gnarlpine Ambushers and return to me.","done":"You have served the good people of Dolanaar and Darnassus well, brave ‹class›. As a member of the Sentinel force of Teldrassil I salute your efforts.","pins":[{"z":"Teldrassil","x":54.6,"y":58.5,"n":"Moon Priestess Amara","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["teldrassil"]},"99047":{"id":99047,"t":"Not dead yet","lv":9,"min":4,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Seek aid from Byancie in Dolaanar for Sentinel Eralya Leafshadow.","desc":"My sisters and I... were dispatched... Oracle Tree...\nTree... message. I... harpies... everywhere...\n<Eralya coughs up blood, grimacing through the pain.>\nI may not have long... no one coming. Please... Byancie... in Dolanaar...","done":"The harpies have become afflicted by the same foulness showing up throughout the forest. I'm sure that is what ails Sentinel Eralya as well.\nWe must hurry. It won't be long before she succumbs to her injuries.","pins":[{"z":"Teldrassil","x":37.6,"y":36.8,"n":"Sentinel Eralya Leafshadow","s":1},{"z":"Teldrassil","x":55.2,"y":56.8,"n":"Byancie","e":1}],"cats":["teldrassil"]},"887":{"id":887,"t":"Southsea Freebooters","lv":14,"min":9,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Kill 12 Southsea Brigands and 6 Southsea Cannoneers for Gazlowe in Ratchet.\nSouthsea Brigand slain : 0/ 12\nSouthsea Cannoneer slain : 0/ 6","desc":"I sure wish Vice Admiral Grezzlik did a better job of keeping the seas safe for our trading vessels. With all the gold the trade princes have poured into the Trade Fleets, it ticks me off to see so many pirates running willy-nilly, raiding my ships and stealing my goods!\nI heard that the Southsea Freebooters have set up a camp just south of here. They've been a real thorn in my side and if Grezzlik won't take care of them, well, maybe you can help me get rid of them.","rew":"Money: 5 0 gold, 5 silver, 0 copper Experience: 750\n+75 reputation with Ratchet","back":"I don't even want to think about the profits I've lost from pirate raiding, and now they set up camp on my doorstep? It's getting out of hand, Undermine's got to do something about it.","done":"You did good, kid. A little more work like that, and it'll be one less thing I'll have to worry about. Hopefully they'll be convinced that they should relocate their operation elsewhere.\nIn the meantime, there is the small matter of getting back the goods they stole from me!","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":62.7,"y":36.2,"n":"Gazlowe","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["the-barrens"]},"167":{"id":167,"t":"Oh Brother. . .","lv":20,"min":15,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Renamed from Oh Brother. . . New rewards: Miner's Workgloves, Miner's Workboots. Partly read from what the game server sent.","obj":"Bring Foreman Thistlenettle's Explorers' League Badge to Wilder Thistlenettle in Stormwind.\nThistlenettle's Badge Foreman Thistlenettle","desc":"We were deep in a vast mine in Westfall, hidden beneath a barn in Moonbrook. No clue where these stinkin' thieving types came from. Anyway, the mine tunnel collapsed on us. I got out but the others... well... the others haven't been heard from.\nYou look like you might have better luck in there. If you could look for my brother, I'd be thankful. He always carried his Explorers' League Badge. If you can't find him, that badge would at least give me some peace of mind.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nMiner's Revenge Miner's Workgloves Miner's Workboots\nNew in Forever: Miner's Workgloves, Miner's Workboots.\nExperience: 1,550\n+100 reputation with Ironforge","back":"Did you find any sign of my brother? Is there any hope after all this time?","done":"My suspicions were correct. My poor brother.... Well, thank you for bringing some conclusion to this mystery, even if the conclusion was grim.\nStormwind City Westfall","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":70.3,"y":40.8,"n":"Wilder Thistlenettle","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["the-deadmines"]},"7847":{"id":7847,"t":"Return to Primal Torntusk","lv":51,"min":46,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Elder Torntusk at Jintha'alor wants you to return to Primal Torntusk at Revantusk Village with news of his rescue.","desc":"Return to my mate, Primal Torntusk at Revantusk Village. Tell her that I am coming home! She is sure to reward you.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nHighland Bow Flask of Forest Mojo\nMoney: 2 25 2 gold, 25 silver, 0 copper Experience: 4,900\n+200 reputation with Revantusk Trolls","done":"You have done the Revantusk a great service, ‹name›! We owe you a great debt of gratitude.","pins":[{"z":"The Hinterlands","x":59.7,"y":77.8,"n":"Elder Torntusk","s":1},{"z":"The Hinterlands","x":78.2,"y":81.2,"n":"Primal Torntusk","e":1}],"cats":["the-hinterlands"]},"2967":{"id":2967,"t":"Return to Thunder Bluff","lv":50,"min":45,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Nara Wildmane in Thunder Bluff.\nMiniature Platinum Discs\nProvided: Miniature Platinum Discs","desc":"You access the pedestal again; the platinum discs suddenly appear once more in your backpack.\nWith the knowledge of the stone watcher learned and the discs returned to your possession, the time has come to return to Thunder Bluff and inform the Nara Wildmane of your discovery.","rew":"Experience: 470\n+10 reputation with Thunder Bluff","back":"Welcome back ‹name›. Were you able to use the discs to your advantage, or was it for naught?","done":"You were missing some discs? Interestingly enough, it seems that the discs of Norgannon are only parts of the complete set - like keys on a key ring, if you will.\nIf we can find the Plates of Uldum, then we could actually access the Uldum complex itself. I don't know whether to be excited by that prospect, or be terrified.\nWe may need to risk everything to ensure that those secrets the earth keeps which would destroy us all remain just that - secrets.\nTanaris Thunder Bluff","pins":[{"z":"Tanaris","x":37.6,"y":81.4,"n":"Uldum Pedestal","s":1},{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":75.6,"y":31.6,"n":"Nara Wildmane","e":1}],"cats":["thunder-bluff"]},"5847":{"id":5847,"t":"Welcome!","lv":1,"min":1,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Deathknell Gift Voucher to Claire Willower in Deathknell.\nDeathknell Gift Voucher\nProvided: Deathknell Gift Voucher","desc":"Welcome to the World of Warcraft!\nAs special thanks for purchasing the World of Warcraft Collector's Edition, turn in this gift voucher to Claire Willower in Deathknell. You'll then be given a gift: a little companion to join you on your quest for adventure and glory.\nThanks again, and enjoy your stay in the World of Warcraft!","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nDiablo Stone Panda Collar Zergling Leash","back":"Greetings! It is a pleasure to meet you!\nI see you have a special voucher. Give it to me and I will offer you something in exchange.","done":"You are indeed a special hero, ‹name›. We welcome you to the world of Azeroth, and offer you one of these unique gifts!","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":32.1,"y":66.5,"n":"Claire Willower","e":1}],"cats":["tirisfal-glades"]},"407":{"id":407,"t":"Fields of Grief","lv":7,"min":4,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take the Laced Pumpkin to the Captured Scarlet Zealot who is being held in the cellar of the Gallow's End Tavern.\nLaced Pumpkin\nProvided: Laced Pumpkin","desc":"Harmless pumpkins, right? Or so it would seem. If we are to defeat Arthas's advances from the North and the Human infestation from the South we need to start realizing the full potential of our gift of undeath.\nWith a little ingenuity a simple pumpkin becomes an agent for our Dark Lady. This pumpkin, laced with my latest formula, will prove to be quite a treat.\nYet another Scarlet Zealot has been captured and is being kept in the cellar of the Gallow's End Tavern. Take this pumpkin to the fool.","rew":"Experience: 160\n+25 reputation with Undercity","back":"Stay away, foul and unholy creature! May the Light protect me! The Scarlet Crusade shall rid Azeroth of your. . .\n. . .oh wait. Is that food for me? I am so hungry. . .","done":"By the Light! Finally some food! Sweet, sweet pumpkin. . . .","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":59.4,"y":52.4,"n":"Apothecary Johaan","s":1},{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":62,"y":51.3,"n":"Captured Scarlet Zealot","e":1}],"cats":["tirisfal-glades"]},"4967":{"id":4967,"t":"Knowledge of the Orb of Orahil","lv":35,"min":35,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak to Menara Voidrender in the Barrens.","desc":"Still a fool, and still seeking the trappings of mortals. Yes, I speak to you with arrogance. I see you before me and I laugh. You're pathetic!\nBut it matters not what I think. It only matters what those willing to deal with you thinks! And in this case, against my better judgment, those with some portion of power feel you deserve more.\nIf this is something you strive for then you should speak with Menara Voidrender in the tower above Ratchet. I believe you have met her before some time ago.","rew":"Experience: 1,350","done":"Ah, you do seek something more... substantial. That I can help you if you truly are prepared.\nIt's a welcome change to see one of our kind seeking more power in forms other than just knowledge.\nSo, do you feel you're ready, ‹name›?\nOrgrimmar The Barrens","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":48.5,"y":45.4,"n":"Zevrost","s":1},{"z":"The Barrens","x":62.5,"y":35.4,"n":"Menara Voidrender","e":1}],"cats":["warlock"]},"4487":{"id":4487,"t":"Summon Felsteed","lv":40,"min":40,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak to Strahad Farsan in Ratchet.","desc":"Ah, good, you're here. I sent a succubus/infernal after you to get your attention, but it seems you were able to get here before it found you. No matter.\nThere has been some talk lately of your growing power--that is good for you, possibly bad for others. But those are irrelevant points. The point is, I feel you've proven yourself and therefore are deserving of... hehe... a blessing of sorts.\nAbove Ratchet in the Barrens you'll find a man named Strahad. I believe you've crossed paths before.\nDun Morogh The Barrens","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":59.2,"y":22,"n":"Briarthorn","s":1},{"z":"The Barrens","x":62.6,"y":35.5,"n":"Strahad Farsan","e":1}],"cats":["warlock"]},"1847":{"id":1847,"t":"Brutal Legguards","lv":30,"min":20,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","rew":"You will receive:\nBrutal Legguards\nExperience: 1,850","done":"Here are your legguards, ‹name›. Let me know how they fit or if you need any modifications. I aim to please! At least I used to.\nThese days I don't care much for my craft. But it beats being a mindless minion of the Scourge!\nI guess.","pins":[{"z":"Undercity","x":62.1,"y":39.1,"n":"Velora Nitely","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["warrior"]},"8567":{"id":8567,"t":"Past Victories in Warsong Gulch","lv":1,"min":1,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Silverwing Talisman of Merit","desc":"Ah, yes! Of course we wouldn't forget about your past accomplishments in Warsong Gulch.","rew":"You will receive:\n3 Warsong Gulch Mark of Honor\nLevel 1 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 4 6 Side Alliance Shareable Yes Quest ID 8567","cats":["warsong-gulch"]},"8407":{"id":8407,"t":"Fight for Warsong Gulch","lv":59,"min":50,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 3 Warsong Gulch Marks of Honor to an Alliance Brigadier General outside the battlegrounds.\n3 Warsong Gulch Mark of Honor","desc":"The Silverwing Sentinels are at war with the Warsong Outriders due to the destruction the Orcs are causing to the forest. There are, however, more reasons to defend this particular forest than plain love for nature.\nThe forest forms a strategic barrier that makes Ashenvale defendable against a large-scale attack. Without it, Astranaar would last a day or two before being annexed to the Barrens.\nDo your part in fighting the Warsong Outriders, ‹name›! For the Alliance!","rew":"Experience: 3,200\n+50 reputation with Silverwing Sentinels","back":"You've come back with news from the front, ‹name›?","done":"Well done, ‹name›! You've served the Alliance well.\nDun Morogh Darnassus Stormwind City","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":62.3,"y":35.5,"n":"Alliance Brigadier General","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Darnassus","x":58,"y":34.2,"n":"Alliance Brigadier General","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":81.2,"y":38.5,"n":"Alliance Brigadier General","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["warsong-gulch"]},"647":{"id":647,"t":"MacKreel's Moonshine","lv":30,"min":28,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take MacKreel's Moonshine to Brewmeister Bilger in Southshore.\nMacKreel's Moonshine\nProvided: MacKreel's Moonshine","desc":"Had quite a bit of the ol' Moonshine last night! Longbraid would have my head if he knew that I passed out during my watch.\nThe noggin hurts something fierce. Felt as though a whole brigade of siege engines passed overhead, all that rumbling.\nOh my, look at the time! I promised Brewmeister Bilger in Southshore that I'd repay my debt to him by sending some Moonshine.\nBut there are just 15 minutes left before I'm overdue! Take him this batch, would you please? And hurry!","rew":"Money: 55 0 gold, 55 silver, 0 copper Experience: 3,050\n+150 reputation with Ironforge","back":"What's the good word, ‹race›?","done":"Ah, nothing like Foggy MacKreel's Moonshine to warm you up on a brisk day! And here I was thinking the little bugger was going to be overdue on his bills again. Thank you, friend! Many thanks indeed!\nArathi Highlands Hillsbrad Foothills","pins":[{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":43.2,"y":92.6,"n":"Foggy MacKreel","s":1},{"z":"Hillsbrad Foothills","x":52.1,"y":58.7,"n":"Brewmeister Bilger","e":1}],"cats":["wetlands"]},"4807":{"id":4807,"t":"Wildkin E'ko","lv":60,"min":55,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"3 Wildkin E'ko Berserk Owlbeast 20 % , Moontouched Owlbeast 20 % , Crazed Owlbeast 20 % , Ragged Owlbeast 0.9 % and 1 more","rew":"You will receive:\n3 Juju Guile","back":"In Winterspring, you will fight creatures of might dat seem to possess an innate magic ability. These wildkin can use strong magics. If you wish ta gain an increase in your intellect bring me da E'ko you find from any a' da owlbeasts you find der.\nRememba, you must have the Cache of Mau'ari in your inventory if you want ta hunt for E'ko.","done":"Mau'ari can derive da juju for ‹name›... Use da Cache of Mau'ari to cast dis upon yourself or your allies.","pins":[{"z":"Winterspring","x":61.9,"y":38.3,"n":"Witch Doctor Mau'ari","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["winterspring"]},"93927":{"id":93927,"t":"A last request","lv":8,"min":5,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Collect the note you found near the dead peacekeeper and read it to determine your next steps.\nBloody Note\nSkypriest Aanders slain\nRaani's Lucky Feather\nShadowsong Family Signet","desc":"<As you inspect the body of the dead peacekeeper, a bloody note falls free of his hands. Picking it up and reading it may give you a clue as to how to proceed from here.>","rew":"Money: 2 25 0 gold, 2 silver, 25 copper Experience: 525\n+50 reputation with Windshapers\n+50 reputation with High Order","back":"What news from the western watch?","done":"So they are all dead, then. Storms curse on these cult bastards!\nWhile you managed to take out the priest and stop the cultists at the tower, I confess that I'm now doubly concerned about whatever it was you said that they were doing to the pylon. The fact that there was such a massive cache of windstones there with them tells me that they needed enormous energy for it.\nI have to wonder, what's the end goal here? Violating the pylon, attacking the village? To what end?","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":42.4,"y":62,"n":"Peacekeeper Vaaniel","s":1},{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":45.6,"y":45.4,"n":"Constable Aonda","e":1}],"cats":["zephras-isle"]},"92727":{"id":92727,"t":"The missing scholar","lv":10,"min":4,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Discover what became of Fillion Flamebreeze.","desc":"Seeking knowledge is the primary mandate of the High Order, but this work has never been more dangerous than it is now on Zephras.\nOne of our scholars--Fillion Flamebreeze--was en route to the Shen'dar Highlands to study the windborne magic that congregates in some areas there. Regrettably, he has not returned and we fear that something may have befallen him on the road.\nIf you can, please locate him for us. He was last seen on the road leading west from Valanaar towards Shen'dar Highlands.","done":"<The satchel lying before you has a few specks of what appears to be dried blood on the flap. Studying the stain you also notice that the flap also has a name embroidered onto it. It reads \"Fillion Flamebreeze\".>","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":66.2,"y":79.8,"n":"Dondallion Whisperwind","s":1},{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":53.3,"y":72.2,"n":"Bloodstained Satchel","e":1}],"cats":["zephras-isle"]},"94487":{"id":94487,"t":"Unwanted and unworthy","lv":11,"min":8,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Collect 10 Bloodied Heirlooms from Al'Aketh Footsoldiers and Al'Aketh Stormchasers in the Shadowgale Forest.\n10 Bloody Heirloom","desc":"The Al'aketh Cultists ambushed us with no warning, though their motives remain a mystery to me. I knew these cultists had clouds in-between their ears, but I never imagined they would upset the delicate balance here on Zephras with such brutality. Go, slay as many as you can and take their heirlooms if they wear any.\n<Elegael spits.>\nThese storm cursed cultists don't deserve to be called shen'dorei. The beasts of the forest can have their bodies. Their ashes don't deserve the winds.","back":"I will make the cult pay for every drop of druid blood they have spilled this day.","done":"<Elegael looks down at the collection of bloodied heirlooms with distress.>\nSo many young lives with so much potential now gone forever. Thank you for returning these, ‹class›.\nI will hold onto them for safe keeping until I am able to take them to the High Elder. There they can go back into the collection and await the next and perhaps more worthy generation to come of age.","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":61.6,"y":39.2,"n":"Elegael Thornpaw","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["zephras-isle"]},"3527":{"id":3527,"t":"The Prophecy of Mosh'aru","lv":47,"min":40,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the First and Second Mosh'aru Tablets to Yeh'kinya in Tanaris.\nFirst Mosh'aru Tablet Theka the Martyr in Zul'Farrak , Theka the Martyr Shapeshift\nSecond Mosh'aru Tablet Hydromancer Velratha in Zul'Farrak","desc":"The ancient prophecy of Mosh'aru speaks of a way to contain the god Hakkar's essence. It was written on two tablets and taken to the troll city of Zul'Farrak, west of Gadgetzan.\nBring me the Mosh'aru tablets!\nThe first tablet is held by the long-dead troll Theka the Martyr. It is said his persecutors were cursed into scarabs and now scuttle about his shrine.\nThe second tablet is held by the hydromancer Velratha, near the sacred pool of Gahz'rilla.\nWhen you have the tablets, bring them to me.","rew":"Experience: 5,250","back":"Do you have the tablets of the Prophecy of Mosh'aru, ‹name›?\nWhen I gain the tablets, I will study them, and learn how to contain the essence of Hakkar!","done":"Ah, this is good. I can fuse these ancient tablets together, and then study their hidden secrets.\nMy debt to you grows, ‹name›. And it will grow further still.","pins":[{"z":"Tanaris","x":67,"y":22.4,"n":"Yeh'kinya","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["zulfarrak"]}});